🟠 **Nested-block helper-local proxies collapse identity — reintroduces the false-positive overlap.**

`readProvenance(declaration.scopeNode)` only inspects the immediate scope node. For a `const`/`let` proxy declared inside a nested block *inside* a helper (an `if`/`try`/`switch`-case body), `declaration.scopeNode` is that inner `BlockStatement`, which `tagProvenance` never stamped — only the expansion wrapper block (created in `gsapInline.ts:347`) carries the tag.

**Repro:**

```js
const tl = gsap.timeline();
function addDriver(at) {
  if (at >= 0) {                       // any nested block
    const driver = { value: 0 };
    tl.to(driver, { value: 1, duration: 1 }, at);
  }
}
addDriver(0);
addDriver(0.5);
```

Both expansions produce `targetIdentity = "proxy:driver@<sourceStart>"` (empty instance suffix). `packages/lint/src/rules/gsap.ts` sees identical identities + overlapping windows → false-positive `overlapping_gsap_tweens` on what are actually two independent helper-local proxies. This is the exact bug the PR body's invariant *"Helper-local proxy declarations receive per-expansion identity"* claims to fix.

The pre-final-commit code used `readProvenance(call.node)` (the tween call), which `tagTimelineCalls` walks with `walkNodes` and stamps regardless of nesting depth — so nested-block proxies were correctly distinguished. The `20c5ee22` commit that fixed shared-outer proxies traded this away.

**Fix — walk up from `declaration.scopeNode` to the nearest provenance-tagged block.** The primitive already exists at line 527 (`nearestExpandedScopeFromAncestors`), but it takes ancestors of the *usage*, not the declaration. Simplest patch:

```ts
const declarationProvenance =
  readProvenance(declaration.scopeNode) ??
  readProvenance(nearestExpandedScopeAbove(declaration.scopeNode));
```

where `nearestExpandedScopeAbove` walks the AST parents from `declaration.scopeNode` upward until it finds a tagged `BlockStatement`. Missing test — add:

```ts
it("keeps helper-created object proxy instances distinct across nested blocks", () => {
  expectDistinctProxyIdentities(`
    const tl = gsap.timeline();
    function addDriver(at) {
      if (at >= 0) {
        const driver = { value: 0 };
        tl.to(driver, { value: 1, duration: 1 }, at);
      }
    }
    addDriver(0);
    addDriver(0.5);
  `);
});
```

Fails against current HEAD; passes with the ancestor-walk fix.

